 "capsule": "The Kingdom of the Isles, called in Old Norse the Suðreyjar ('Southern Isles') and in Gaelic Innse Gall, was a Norse-Gaelic sea-kingdom that emerged from Viking settlement of the Hebrides and the Isle of Man from the 9th century and crystallized under Godred Crovan, who seized Man in 1079 and founded the dynasty styled Rex Manniae et Insularum. His descendants Olaf I (c.1113-1153) and Godred the Black (1153-1187) ruled the Hebrides and Man as vassals of Norway, but Somerled's naval victory over Godred in 1156 and his expulsion of him in 1158 permanently partitioned the realm: the Crovan kings retained Man and the northern Hebrides while Somerled's descendants held Argyll and the southern isles, leaving the once-unified sea-kingdom divided for good.",
